course: dictionary
lesson: 15507
title: Submerge and submerged
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To submerge something is to put it under water, or to go under water yourself. «The submarine began to submerge slowly.» The submarine is going down under the water, so submerge means to go under.
explain: Submerged describes something that is covered by water. «After the flood, the road was submerged.» The clue is flood: when water covers the road, you cannot see it, so submerged means covered by water.
explain: The word can also mean being completely surrounded by something, such as work or noise. «She was submerged in her book and did not hear the bell.» Her book covered all her attention, so submerged here means completely absorbed.
fact: Submerge is a verb, so it can change: submerges, submerged, submerging.
fact: Submerged is an adjective when it describes something covered by water, as in «a submerged road».
fact: «Submerge» means to go under water, or to put something completely under water or another liquid.
fact: «Submerged» means covered by water. To be submerged in work or noise means to be completely surrounded or overwhelmed by it.
fact: Submarines submerge by filling tanks with water and surface by blowing the water out. Scientists also submerge objects in water to measure their volume.
exercise: «The submarine began to submerge slowly.» What does submerge mean here? | *Go under water | Fly up into the sky | Shine brightly in the sun | Stop moving for ever
exercise: «After the flood, the road was submerged.» Find and copy one word that means covered by water. | flood | the | After | *submerged
exercise: «She was submerged in her book and did not hear the bell.» What does submerged in her book suggest? | She was tired and cold | She had dropped the book in a bath | *Completely absorbed, not noticing things around her | She was swimming in the book
test: «Ella watched the tide rise and slowly submerge the sandcastle.» What does submerge mean? | Build higher | Dry out in the sun | *Cover completely with water | Lift it up into the air
test: Why should you never walk through a submerged road? | The road is too hot | The water makes your shoes shine | *The water can be deeper and faster than it looks | Submerged roads are always new
exam: Which word means covered by water? | *Submerged | Surface | Blowing | Submarine
